<title>USA: Minor N.Mexico coffee areas seen near freezing - WSC.</title>
<headline>Minor N.Mexico coffee areas seen near freezing - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cold air is heading for the north of Mexico and temperatures near freezing in the high-elevation coffee areas may cause some damage, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The main coffee belt at lower elevations should have lows only in the middle or upper 30s F and little damage is expected, it said.</p>
<p>The forecast is for variable clouds with widely scattered to scattered showers and thunderstorms in southern Mexico, but fair and colder conditions in the north.</p>
<p>Low temperatures will drop to near freezing in minor coffee and citrus areas, with some minor damage possible.</p>
<p>On Wednesday Mexico was dry, with highs of 61-93 F.</p>
</text>
